  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"In this book of poems and stories, I sift through a life of memories on the North Shore of Boston, and this is my catch."--Intro.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Artists' book. Hand-made hemp-cotton mix paper. Bound as a double pamphlet; exposed sewing on spine. Illustrations are linoleum block prints. All writing, artwork, printing, and binding was done by Sara Owen in fulfillment of her MFA in Book Arts from the University of Alabama.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Edition of 65 signed copies, library copy is number 14.</subfield>
  </datafield>
